<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0"><head><title>Playing Cairn in Pointliner</title></head><body>
<outline text="# Playing Cairn in Pointliner">
  <outline text="Cairn's system wired into Pointliner pills: saves, damage, slot inventory, and the game's tables, all live in one file. Cairn has no built-in oracle, so pair it with the Oracle play case for yes/no questions. See cairn.md for the walkthrough. The dice and inventory pills are complete, and the tables carry short filler options you replace with the SRD's own entries. Every pill here is live, click one to run it."/>
  <outline text="Adapted from Cairn by Yochai Gal, used under CC BY-SA 4.0 (creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0). Changes made: the tables and procedures are restructured into outline points and pills. Because Cairn is ShareAlike, the adapted Cairn material here is likewise CC BY-SA 4.0 (separate from Pointliner's AGPLv3 app licence). Cairn is named descriptively; no logo or art is reproduced.">
    <outline text="The tables below hold filler options written for this demo, not Cairn's own entries. Replace the filler inside each `{rule ...}` with the entries from your copy of the SRD; every pill is already wired, so a table updates the moment you edit its rule. Reproduced Cairn tables carry the ShareAlike terms."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## A character in three rolls">
    <outline text="Roll three attributes on 3d6 and Hit Protection on 1d6, then set the variables so the rest of the sheet reads them."/>
    <outline text="STR: {3d6}   DEX: {3d6}   WIL: {3d6}"/>
    <outline text="Hit Protection: {1d6}"/>
    <outline text="Set your rolled attributes here: {str := 10}, {dex := 12}, {wil := 9}."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Saves">
    <outline text="Everything risky is a save: roll 1d20 and succeed if it is at or under the attribute. Change a stat above and every save that reads it updates.">
      <outline text="Strength save: {1d20} (success if at or under str, which is {str})"/>
      <outline text="Dexterity save: {1d20} (success if at or under dex, which is {dex})"/>
      <outline text="Willpower save: {1d20} (success if at or under wil, which is {wil})"/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Inventory and encumbrance">
    <outline text="Cairn's inventory is a slot system. Each item carries a slots property, the pack totals them, and a check flags an overload. The total sits on the Pack point itself, because a rollup reads the points BELOW it: as a sibling of the items it would find nothing. Add the check from the Pack point's bullet menu (Add check) or with /check.">
      <outline text="Pack, {= sum(slots)} of 10 slots used" _props="[{&quot;key&quot;:&quot;check&quot;,&quot;val&quot;:&quot;sum(slots) &lt;= 10&quot;}]">
        <outline text="Sword {prop slots: 1}"/>
        <outline text="Torches, three {prop slots: 1}"/>
        <outline text="Rope, fifty feet {prop slots: 1}"/>
        <outline text="Rations {prop slots: 1}"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Damage">
    <outline text="Damage hits Hit Protection first, then Strength; low Strength means Strength saves to avoid dying. Roll the weapon die, take armour off, then read the rest against your HP and STR.">
      <outline text="Blade: {1d8}   Club: {1d6}   Bow: {1d6}"/>
      <outline text="A monster hits you for {1d6}. Subtract armour, take the rest off HP, then off STR."/>
      <outline text="When Strength runs low, save to hold on: {1d20} at or under str ({str})."/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## The game's tables">
    <outline text="Each table is a weighted pick. Declare one with the rule keyword, as `{rule name: option | option}`, then call it by name anywhere. A bare `name: option | option` is ordinary text and registers nothing. Replace the filler options with the SRD's entries, separated by bars; use weights to match a 2d6 table's distribution."/>
    <outline text="{rule reaction: hostile | wary | neutral | curious | helpful}"/>
    <outline text="{rule omen: a cold draft | distant scratching | a fresh corpse | scratched warnings}"/>
    <outline text="Ask the room: reaction is {reaction}; an omen in the dark is {omen}."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Run it yourself">
    <outline text="Roll the three {3d6} attributes and {1d6} HP, then set the variables. Roll {1d20} for a save and read it against the attribute. Add items with a slots property and watch the Pack check go red when overloaded. Roll a weapon die, take damage off HP then STR, and save when Strength runs low. Add the tables you use most, and it is your Cairn character."/>
  </outline>
</outline>
</body></opml>
